      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوصَدٌ</span></b>  A door, or entrance, <i>closed:</i> (L:) or
<i>become closed.</i> (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  In the Kur, eiv. 8, [and
xc. 20,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوصَدَةٌ</span> (as some read instead of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤْصَدَةٌ</span>,
L) signifies <i>Closed over.</i> (S, L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَصِيدٌ</span>.

